    "description": "Zenitcopy 3D-6L Skeletonized M-Lok Handstop V1.1: Laffs\n\nVariant of the original Laffs Dynamics Zenitcopy 3D-6L handstop. (Itself being a copy of the Zenitco RK-6L)\n\nSkeletonized for max style points, and for that .01oz weight savings you just HAD to have... \n\n\nUpdate V1.1: Thickened inside walls by 1mm, (Including lower skeletonized struts.) reduced designer's logo size, shortened M-Lok interface by .25mm.\n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 218C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .12mm\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 7+\nInfill: 50%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 18%\n\n\n\nHardware Needed:\n\n1x M5x10 Hex Socketed Machine Screw/Bolt\n\n1x M-Lok T-Nut (Be sure both bolt & nut are the same thread pitch.)\n\n\n\nOriginal Zenticopy 3D-6L can be found here: https://odysee.com/@FFFTech:3/Zenitcopy-3D-6L:e\n\nTougher SLS Nylon Zenitcope 3D-6L can be purchased here: https://www.avesrails.com/Zenitcope-3D-6L-M-LOK-Handstop_p_89.html",
